-- title:
--   An element of C[J/varpiₜ] outside every Igusa-type valuation ring
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and assume $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — by definition the kernel of the reduction map of unit groups out of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ attached to the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'` — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{\times}$ coming from $\ell \mid M' \mid q^2M'$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((T))$ given by [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain which is a henselian local ring with algebraically closed residue field, with $L$ as its fraction field, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$; let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the classical $j$-function with coefficients transported from $\mathbb{Q}$ to $L$. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$, and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the chart algebra, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and write $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout of the two affine charts, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and the morphism `ιFin` from $\operatorname{Spec} C$.
--
--   Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $\varpi$, and assume (`hss`) that $y$ is supersingular: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $x \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $x$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-chart block.** The hypothesis `hArig` asserts the following for every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$, and every such $y'$ satisfying the supersingularity condition of `hss` for its own prime ideal: there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units and
--   $$f \equiv X_0X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q}X_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}},$$
--   ($X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto
--   $$S := W[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})\,v - f\,u\big),$$
--   such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the canonical map $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ determined by $y'$, the following seven clauses hold.
--
--   (1) *Constants*: for every $a \in A$, the image under $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ of the germ of $a$ is the constant series $\sigma a$ in $S$.
--
--   (2) *Stability of the chart*: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — the condition that for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ for the level group attached to $H_1$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g$ nonzero, and every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is that of $f/g$, the series of $\tau x$ read through any embedding $\iota$ of $L$ into $\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$ satisfies $\iota(\tau x)\cdot \mathrm{qExp}(g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}) = \mathrm{qExp}(f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})$ — the automorphism $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$.
--
--   (3) *Triviality of the diamond*: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ and every $\tau$ as in (2), the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo the prime of $y'$: $\tau a - a \in y'$ for all $a \in C$.
--
--   (4) *Equivariance of the chart*: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau$ as in (2) preserving $C$ and inducing the identity modulo the prime of $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{M}_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwines the action of $\tau|_C$ with $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$; $\theta$ fixes every constant $w \in W$; $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the images of $X_0, X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$, modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; if $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ then $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ while $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$, then $c - 1 \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   (5) *Separation of branches*: for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of the images of $X_0, X_1$, each containing the constant $\sigma\varpi$, and each containing an element of the shape $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct.
--
--   (6) *Recognition of a branch*: for every prime $P$ of $S$ omitting at least one of the images of $X_0, X_1$, containing the constant $\sigma\varpi$, and containing an element $1\cdot X_0 + 0\cdot X_1 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a \in C$: the image of the germ of $a$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ (as an element of $K \subseteq L((T))$) lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ in $L$.
--
--   (7) *Hasse-invariant clause*: the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $q$-fold rescaling `qExpand L q` of `jqModC L`) lies in $K$ and in $C$; there are $a_0 \in A$ with this element congruent to $a_0$ modulo the prime of $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that, for all $a, b \in W$ of which at least one is a unit and with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, the element $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^i b^{\,e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W$, and such that $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ sends the germ of the element `jqNModC L q` $- a_0$ of $C$ to the class of $h$ in $S$.
--
--   **The point and its explicit chart.** Fix a point $z$ of $X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the global section coming from $\varpi$ along `toBase`, assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ carried to $z$ by `ιFin`, satisfying the supersingularity condition of `hss` for its prime ideal, with $y' = y$ as ideals of $C$. Fix, moreover, a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ with $S_1 := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW_1` asserts that this datum satisfies the seven clauses (1)–(7) above at $z$ and $y'$.
--
--   **Blow-up chart.** Let $J \subseteq C$ be the infimum (`hJ`) of the family of ideals obtained, as $\gamma$ runs over $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the $L$-algebra automorphisms of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` at $\gamma^{-1}$ and preserving $C$, by pulling back along $\tau|_C$ the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained (`hB`) by adjoining to $C$ the set $\{x \in K : x\,\varpi_t \in J\}$, that is $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$.
--
--   Let $\mathcal{W}$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and assume three further groups of hypotheses. `hR1`: $C \subseteq B$, and $K$ is the fraction field of $B$ (every $f \in K$ is $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$). `hR2`: $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): an element of $L$ lies in $\mathcal{W}$ if and only if it comes from $A$; the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{W}$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $\mathcal{W}$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element $b \in C$ lies in $y$ if and only if it lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{W}$; and $f \in K$ lies in $\mathcal{W}$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h$ a unit of $\mathcal{W}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exists $b \in K$ with $b \in B$ such that, for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ satisfying
--
--   - $V \cap L = A$, in the sense that an element of $L$ lies in $V$ if and only if it comes from $A$;
--
--   - whenever the image of $\varpi$ lies in $V$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $V$;
--
--   - $j \in V$, and for every monic polynomial $p$ over $A$ such that the value at $j$ of the image of $p$ in $K[t]$ lies in $V$, that value is not in the maximal ideal of $V$ (so every monic polynomial expression in $j$ which is regular at $V$ is a unit there),
--
--   one has $b \notin V$.
--
--   This is the pole clause for the blown-up chart $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$ at a supersingular point of the two-chart integral model: it exhibits a regular function on the blow-up which fails to be regular at any valuation of Igusa type, those valuations restricting to $A$ on $L$ at which $j$ is a unit-generic parameter. It is the input used by the companion orbit-pole statement of the same auxiliary level-one frame (the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond variant with $\ell \equiv 11 \bmod 12$, $\ell \mid M'$), in the construction of the integral model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$.
